// Reducer for the associative-literal parser HANG: a keyed element in a
// value literal must ERROR LOUDLY (naming the gap), never spin. The
// ctor-args element loop owns the ',' / close separator grammar;
// parseExpression pushes a bare ':' back (the ternary-branch pushback
// convention), and without the loop's wall the same token re-headed
// parseExpression forever — SIGKILL by the CPU cap, no diagnostics.
// Oracle: g++ `std::vector<int> v{1: 2};` -> "expected '}' before ':'";
// clang++ -> "expected '}'". madc names the gap and the road instead.
int main()
{
	var m = { "a": 1 };
	return 0;
}
